<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Flexbox & Grid Responsive Layout</title>
    <!-- Load Tailwind CSS -->
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <style>
        /* Custom font setup */
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@100..900&display=swap');
        body {
            font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
        }
        /* Custom utility for visual clarity on grid/flex areas */
        .shadow-glow {
            box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(120, 80, 255, 0.4);
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 min-h-screen">

    <!-- 
      SECTION 1: HEADER (Flexbox for Centering and Alignment) 
      Demonstrates simple centered content regardless of screen size.
    -->
    <header class="bg-gray-800 p-8 shadow-2xl">
        <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-indigo-400 mb-2">Adaptive Web Layout</h1>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-400">Precision alignment using modern CSS tools (Grid and Flex).</p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main class="max-w-7xl mx-auto p-6 space-y-12">

        <!-- USER INFO BAR (Flexbox for horizontal distribution) -->
        <section class="bg-gray-700 p-4 rounded-xl shadow-lg border-l-4 border-indigo-500">
            <!-- Flexbox: Horizontally space items and vertically center them -->
            <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-between items-start md:items-center space-y-2 md:space-y-0">
                <div class="flex items-center space-x-3">
                    <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-yellow-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"></path></svg>
                    <span class="text-lg font-semibold">Current Viewport: Responsive Grid Demo</span>
                </div>
                <button class="bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white font-medium py-2 px-4 rounded-lg transition duration-200 shadow-md">
                    View Details
                </button>
            </div>
        </section>


        <!-- 
          SECTION 2: MAIN CONTENT (CSS Grid for Responsive Columns) 
          This is the core demonstration of responsive Grid layout.
        -->
        <section>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-gray-700 pb-2">CSS Grid Multi-Column Layout</h2>
            
            <!-- 
              Grid Container Configuration:
              - Mobile (default): grid-cols-1
              - Tablet (md:): md:grid-cols-2 (2 columns)
              - Desktop (lg:): lg:grid-cols-3 (3 columns)
            -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
                
                <!-- Grid Item 1: Uses Flexbox internally for precise vertical centering -->
                <div class="bg-gray-800 p-6 rounded-xl shadow-xl shadow-indigo-900/50 h-64 flex flex-col justify-between">
                    <div>
                        <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-400 uppercase">Feature A</span>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-1">Mobile Stack (1 Col)</h3>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Internal Flexbox: Aligns items vertically at the bottom -->
                    <div class="text-gray-400 text-sm flex items-center mt-4">
                        <span class="p-2 bg-indigo-500 rounded-full w-8 h-8 flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-xs mr-2">1</span>
                        Resizes to fill 50% width on tablet.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Grid Item 2: Uses Flexbox internally for precise vertical centering -->
                <div class="bg-gray-800 p-6 rounded-xl shadow-xl shadow-indigo-900/50 h-64 flex flex-col justify-between">
                    <div>
                        <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-400 uppercase">Feature B</span>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-1">Tablet Half (2 Cols)</h3>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Internal Flexbox: Aligns items vertically at the bottom -->
                    <div class="text-gray-400 text-sm flex items-center mt-4">
                        <span class="p-2 bg-indigo-500 rounded-full w-8 h-8 flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-xs mr-2">2</span>
                        Takes 33.3% width on desktop.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Grid Item 3: Uses Flexbox internally for precise vertical centering -->
                <div class="bg-gray-800 p-6 rounded-xl shadow-xl shadow-indigo-900/50 h-64 flex flex-col justify-between">
                    <div>
                        <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-400 uppercase">Feature C</span>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-1">Desktop Third (3 Cols)</h3>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Internal Flexbox: Aligns items vertically at the bottom -->
                    <div class="text-gray-400 text-sm flex items-center mt-4">
                        <span class="p-2 bg-indigo-500 rounded-full w-8 h-8 flex items-center justify-center text-white font-bold text-xs mr-2">3</span>
                        Uses CSS Grid for outer structure.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Grid Item 4: A wider item to demonstrate variable width in the grid -->
                <div class="bg-gray-800 p-6 rounded-xl shadow-xl shadow-indigo-900/50 h-64 lg:col-span-2 flex flex-col justify-center items-center text-center">
                    <h3 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-green-400">Grid Span Example</h3>
                    <p class="text-lg text-gray-400 mt-2">This block spans two columns on desktop (`lg:col-span-2`).</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Grid Item 5 -->
                <div class="bg-gray-800 p-6 rounded-xl shadow-xl shadow-indigo-900/50 h-64 flex flex-col justify-end">
                    <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-400 uppercase">Feature D</span>
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-1">Auto-Flowing Content</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-2">The grid handles the flow of items naturally when screen size changes.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>


        <!-- 
          SECTION 3: FEATURE ROW (Flexbox for Wrapping and Dynamic Widths) 
          Demonstrates using Flexbox to manage wrapping cards.
        -->
        <section class="mt-12">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 border-b border-gray-700 pb-2">Flexbox Feature Row (Wrapping)</h2>

            <!-- 
              Flex Container Configuration:
              - flex-wrap allows items to stack/wrap
              - gap-6 provides spacing
            -->
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6 justify-center lg:justify-start">

                <!-- Flex Item 1 -->
                <div class="bg-gray-800 p-4 rounded-lg shadow-xl w-full md:w-[48%] lg:w-[31.5%]">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-indigo-300">Item 1</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">This card takes full width on mobile, and approximately 1/3rd width on large screens. It's built with Flexbox for its container.</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Flex Item 2 -->
                <div class="bg-gray-800 p-4 rounded-lg shadow-xl w-full md:w-[48%] lg:w-[31.5%]">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-indigo-300">Item 2</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">Note how the widths are calculated to account for the gap (`gap-6` in Tailwind is 1.5rem or 24px) for perfect alignment.</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Flex Item 3 -->
                <div class="bg-gray-800 p-4 rounded-lg shadow-xl w-full md:w-[48%] lg:w-[31.5%]">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-indigo-300">Item 3</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">On tablets (`md:`), only two items fit per row, causing the third to wrap neatly below. This uses the `flex-wrap` property.</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Flex Item 4 (Optional extra to force wrapping on smaller screens) -->
                 <div class="bg-gray-800 p-4 rounded-lg shadow-xl w-full md:w-[48%] lg:w-[31.5%] hidden md:block">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-indigo-300">Item 4 (MD/LG Only)</h3>
                    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-1">This item is hidden on mobile (`hidden`), but appears on tablet (`md:block`) and desktop for further testing the wrap logic.</p>
                </div>

            </div>
        </section>
        
    </main>

    <!-- 
      SECTION 4: FOOTER (Flexbox for simple layout/alignment) 
    -->
    <footer class="bg-gray-800 mt-12 py-6 border-t border-gray-700">
        <!-- Flexbox: Horizontally center the content -->
        <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto flex justify-center items-center">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
                &copy; 2024 Layout Demo | Built with Flexbox and CSS Grid
            </p>
        </div>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
